.TH CLAUDE-USAGE-EXPORTER 1 "2026-11-27" "claude-usage-exporter 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
claude-usage-exporter \- Prometheus exporter for Claude plan usage limits
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B claude-usage-exporter
.RB [ \-\-bind
.IR ADDR ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR PORT ]
.RB [ \-\-cache\-seconds
.IR N ]
.RB [ \-\-credentials
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-once ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B claude-usage-exporter
reads the Claude CLI's OAuth login and serves the plan's usage windows (the
numbers Claude Code shows under /usage) as Prometheus metrics on
.BI http:// ADDR : PORT /metrics\fR.
The usage endpoint is queried at most once per cache period, whatever the
scrape rate. The endpoint is undocumented; when its answer can't be read the
exporter reports
.B claude_usage_up 0
and keeps serving the login health metrics.
.PP
Only timestamps are read from the credentials file and exported. Token values
are never exported or logged. The exporter never refreshes the token itself:
the Claude CLI does that when it runs.
.SH OPTIONS
Every option can also be set with an environment variable; the option wins.
.TP
.BI \-\-bind " ADDR"
Address to listen on. Environment: CLAUDE_USAGE_BIND. Default: 127.0.0.1.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " PORT"
Port to listen on. Environment: CLAUDE_USAGE_PORT. Default: 9101.
.TP
.BI \-\-cache\-seconds " N"
Query the usage endpoint at most every N seconds. Environment:
CLAUDE_USAGE_CACHE. Default: 300.
.TP
.BI \-\-credentials " FILE"
The Claude CLI credentials file. Environment: CLAUDE_USAGE_CREDENTIALS.
Default: $CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/.credentials.json, or ~/.claude/.credentials.json.
.TP
.BI \-\-url " URL"
Usage endpoint, for testing against a mock server. Environment: CLAUDE_USAGE_URL.
.TP
.B \-\-once
Print the metrics once to standard output and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/default/claude-usage-exporter
Environment defaults for both systemd units.
.TP
.I ~/.config/claude-usage-exporter/env
Per-user overrides for the user unit.
.TP
.I /etc/claude-usage-exporter/USER.env
Per-instance overrides for claude-usage-exporter@USER.service.
.TP
.I /usr/share/claude-usage-exporter/claude-usage-dashboard.json
Grafana dashboard for these metrics.
.SH SYSTEMD
Nothing is enabled when the package is installed. For one user:
.PP
.nf
.RS
systemctl \-\-user daemon\-reload
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now claude\-usage\-exporter
sudo loginctl enable\-linger $USER
.RE
.fi
.PP
Or as a system service running as that user:
.PP
.nf
.RS
sudo systemctl enable \-\-now claude\-usage\-exporter@alice
.RE
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR systemctl (1),
.BR loginctl (1)
.PP
https://github.com/jfryman/claude-usage-exporter
